# Egress allowlist (POSIX extended regex, matched against the destination host).
# FilterDefaultDeny=Yes in tinyproxy.conf means ONLY hosts matching a line here are
# reachable; every other destination is denied. Each entry is anchored to ONE exact
# FQDN (^...$) so this stays a NAMED-DOMAIN allowlist, never an allow-all.
#
# Hostnames are the exact endpoints the matching litellm provider route connects to
# (API-key auth — none of these use a separate OAuth/token host). To enable another
# provider, add one anchored line; keep the list as short as the run needs.
#
# provider     litellm route   key env var
# ----------   -------------   -----------------
# Anthropic    anthropic/      ANTHROPIC_API_KEY
^api\.anthropic\.com$
# OpenAI       openai/         OPENAI_API_KEY
^api\.openai\.com$
# Google Gemini gemini/        GEMINI_API_KEY        (AI Studio REST; NOT Vertex)
^generativelanguage\.googleapis\.com$
# DeepSeek     deepseek/       DEEPSEEK_API_KEY
^api\.deepseek\.com$
# OpenRouter   openrouter/     OPENROUTER_API_KEY
^openrouter\.ai$
#
# NOTE: Vertex AI / Bedrock are intentionally NOT enabled — they need OAuth/SigV4
# token endpoints (e.g. oauth2.googleapis.com, sts.*.amazonaws.com) and provider
# SDKs baked in. Add those hosts here AND the SDK in the Dockerfile if you enable them.
